<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Epsom Derby</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1780–</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as The Derby Stakes</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Epsom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derby">Derby</a> is a flat horse race for three-year-old colts and fillies run each year over about a mile and a half at Epsom Downs in Surrey, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. First run in 1780 and named after the 12th <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/earl-of-derby">Earl of Derby</a>, it is the most prestigious race of the British flat season. In 1934 it was won by Windsor Lad, owned by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of Rajpipla, the first Indian owner to win it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/epsom-derby.jpg" alt="Epsom Derby" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Théodore Géricault · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jean_Louis_Th%C3%A9odore_G%C3%A9ricault_001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
